.SH NAME
Dokumentacja katalogu C:/PinterestApp/WebPhotoPage/Frontend/node_modules/@vitejs/plugin-react
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Opis szczegółowy"
.PP 

.SH "@vitejs/plugin-react [![npm](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@vitejs/plugin-react.svg)](https://npmjs.com/package/@vitejs/plugin-react)"
.PP
The default Vite plugin for React projects\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
enable \fRFast Refresh\fP in development (requires react >= 16\&.9)
.IP "\(bu" 2
use the \fRautomatic JSX runtime\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
use custom Babel plugins/presets
.IP "\(bu" 2
small installation size
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
// vite\&.config\&.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin\-react'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
})
.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
.SS "include/exclude"
Includes \fR\&.js\fP, \fR\&.jsx\fP, \fR\&.ts\fP & \fR\&.tsx\fP and excludes \fR/node_modules/\fP by default\&. This option can be used to add fast refresh to \fR\&.mdx\fP files:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin\-react'
import mdx from '@mdx\-js/rollup'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    { enforce: 'pre', \&.\&.\&.mdx() },
    react({ include: /\\\&.(mdx|js|jsx|ts|tsx)$/ }),
  ],
})
.fi
.PP
.SS "jsxImportSource"
Control where the JSX factory is imported from\&. By default, this is inferred from \fRjsxImportSource\fP from corresponding a tsconfig file for a transformed file\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
react({ jsxImportSource: '@emotion/react' })
.fi
.PP
.SS "jsxRuntime"
By default, the plugin uses the \fRautomatic JSX runtime\fP\&. However, if you encounter any issues, you may opt out using the \fRjsxRuntime\fP option\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
react({ jsxRuntime: 'classic' })
.fi
.PP
.SS "babel"
The \fRbabel\fP option lets you add plugins, presets, and \fRother configuration\fP to the Babel transformation performed on each included file\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
react({
  babel: {
    presets: [\&.\&.\&.],
    // Your plugins run before any built\-in transform (eg: Fast Refresh)
    plugins: [\&.\&.\&.],
    // Use \&.babelrc files
    babelrc: true,
    // Use babel\&.config\&.js files
    configFile: true,
  }
})
.fi
.PP

.PP
Note: When not using plugins, only esbuild is used for production builds, resulting in faster builds\&.
.SS "Proposed syntax"
If you are using ES syntax that are still in proposal status (e\&.g\&. class properties), you can selectively enable them with the \fRbabel\&.parserOpts\&.plugins\fP option:

.PP
.PP
.nf
react({
  babel: {
    parserOpts: {
      plugins: ['decorators\-legacy'],
    },
  },
})
.fi
.PP

.PP
This option does not enable \fIcode transformation\fP\&. That is handled by esbuild\&.

.PP
\fBNote:\fP TypeScript syntax is handled automatically\&.

.PP
Here's the \fRcomplete list of Babel parser plugins\fP\&.
.SS "reactRefreshHost"
The \fRreactRefreshHost\fP option is only necessary in a module federation context\&. It enables HMR to work between a remote & host application\&. In your remote Vite config, you would add your host origin:

.PP
.PP
.nf
react({ reactRefreshHost: 'http://localhost:3000' })
.fi
.PP

.PP
Under the hood, this simply updates the React Fash Refresh runtime URL from \fR/@react-refresh\fP to \fRhttp://localhost:3000/@react-refresh\fP to ensure there is only one Refresh runtime across the whole application\&. Note that if you define \fRbase\fP option in the host application, you need to include it in the option, like: \fRhttp://localhost:3000/{base}\fP\&.
.SH "Middleware mode"
.PP
In \fRmiddleware mode\fP, you should make sure your entry \fRindex\&.html\fP file is transformed by Vite\&. Here's an example for an Express server:

.PP
.PP
.nf
app\&.get('/', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    let html = fs\&.readFileSync(path\&.resolve(root, 'index\&.html'), 'utf\-8')

    // Transform HTML using Vite plugins\&.
    html = await viteServer\&.transformIndexHtml(req\&.url, html)

    res\&.send(html)
  } catch (e) {
    return next(e)
  }
})
.fi
.PP

.PP
Otherwise, you'll probably get this error:

.PP
.PP
.nf
Uncaught Error: @vitejs/plugin\-react can't detect preamble\&. Something is wrong\&.
.fi
.PP
.SH "Consistent components exports"
.PP
For React refresh to work correctly, your file should only export React components\&. You can find a good explanation in the \fRGatsby docs\fP\&.

.PP
If an incompatible change in exports is found, the module will be invalidated and HMR will propagate\&. To make it easier to export simple constants alongside your component, the module is only invalidated when their value changes\&.

.PP
You can catch mistakes and get more detailed warning with this \fReslint rule\fP\&. 
